18u7|v|To reduce from a solid to a liquid state, as by heat; to liquefy; as, to melt wax, tallow, or lead; to melt ice or snow. ; Hence: To soften, as by a warming or kindly influence; to relax; to render gentle or susceptible to mild influences; sometimes, in a bad sense, to take away the firmness of; to weaken. ; To be changed from a solid to a liquid state under the influence of heat; as, butter and wax melt at moderate temperatures. ; To dissolve; as, sugar melts in the mouth. ; Hence: To be softened; to become tender, mild, or gentle; also, to be weakened or subdued, as by fear. ; To lose distinct form or outline; to blend. ; To disappear by being dispersed or dissipated; as, the fog melts away.	o:27i2,53,1;29w8,48,2;197b,30,3;1jda,27,4~1jda,27,4;197b,30,3;29w8,48,2;27i2,53,1	d:x5,32,5;1431,7,4;21r7,5,3~x5,32,5;1431,7,4;21r7,5,3
